{"term":"testify","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:1e3e450ba209273d2f","definition":"To make a declaration, or give evidence, under oath.","example":"One witness shall not testify against any person to cause him to die.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["bear witness"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":["retestify","testifiable","testifiee","testilie","testilying","untestified","untestifying"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/testify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3c76dd02e4969dbabd","definition":"To make a statement based on personal knowledge or faith.","example":"We speak that we do know, and testify that we have seen; and ye receive not our witness.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["bear witness"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":["retestify","testifiable","testifiee","testilie","testilying","untestified","untestifying"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/testify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:38cfbf8afc2434cdc0","definition":"To be evidence of.","example":"Paradoxically, the sharp and unambiguous formulas in which Lenin called for the use of terror and denied the possibility of democracy and freedom testified to the fact that freedom had not yet been completely eradicated.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["bear witness"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":["retestify","testifiable","testifiee","testilie","testilying","untestified","untestifying"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/testify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈtɛstɪfaɪ/"},"wor